{"title":"Mock AIME 6 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_6_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider two circles of different sizes that do not intersect.  The smaller circle has center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  Label the intersection of their common external tangents <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  A common internal tangent intersects the common external tangents at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.  Given that the radius of the larger circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/e/0aed25764bd483c2a8d829e272b6e779508f3131.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PO=3$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f86f6d5842b54e715f632f1975aa8f0b363fd90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=20\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />, what is the square of the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/a/6fa9504a38a8776b653e086a2424cbfb86c3bb7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PBA$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_6_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Mock_AIME_6_P13a.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/dc/Mock_AIME_6_P13a.png/600px-Mock_AIME_6_P13a.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"282\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/dc/Mock_AIME_6_P13a.png/900px-Mock_AIME_6_P13a.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/dc/Mock_AIME_6_P13a.png/1200px-Mock_AIME_6_P13a.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d57520c955e93fed5ad4fd2f528453da3c9b84a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|AB|=|CD|=20\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the distance between centers, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/564371147a9188d484c67d021ef6ae1760f9e480.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h=|PO|=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/f/d1f837f79f1becbe431d256bcdf7b7511b720acc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|CD|^2+(r_2-r_1)^2=d^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b92392d33c2934425f6aaed81bf7b473bdb76630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(20\\sqrt{2})^2+(r_2-r_1)^2=d^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"24\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/f/dff156b83c27bda35f658e009d0e4ebee42ea894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$800+(r_2-r_1)^2=d^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"21\" /> [Equation 1]\n</p><p>By similar triangles,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/6/7e6df2ae61431a43730fc2b5d37ac48610ae04dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{r_1}{h}=\\frac{r_2}{h+d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"92\" height=\"36\" />\n</p><p>solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f836156108bc8b960bbd1e36e9b133ff7cb8acbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\frac{(r_2-r_1)h}{r_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"118\" height=\"43\" /> [Equation 2]\n</p><p>Substituting [Equation 2] into [Equation 1] we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/b/0bb2f01dbfb5d1e49479252e849acf1acb8f672e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$800+(r_2-r_1)^2=\\frac{(r_2-r_1)^2h^2}{r_1^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"248\" height=\"45\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/b/6dbd7bd0cd6e851990803dfef85658adf8009393.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$800+(11-r_1)^2=\\frac{9(11-r_1)^2}{r_1^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"244\" height=\"45\" /> \n</p><p>Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/4/21401c1c7dd0edc1660bb37061550ce58abf5e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> is the radius of the incircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/6/346ebe66934d3d080efb503c06d2dbd680fcf9bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta PBA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> then,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/c/68c1131860eae72503ab3f674afb7e5b5325eeab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1=\\frac{A_1}{s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"39\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/6/346ebe66934d3d080efb503c06d2dbd680fcf9bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta PBA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is half the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/6/346ebe66934d3d080efb503c06d2dbd680fcf9bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta PBA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d2533e7124fac98b94ab75a659e3a498d3320796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1=r_1s=s=\\frac{|AB|+(\\sqrt{(h+d)^2-r_2^2}-k)+(\\sqrt{h^2-r_1^2}+k)}{2}=\\frac{20\\sqrt{2}+\\left( \\frac{r_2}{r_1}+1 \\right)\\sqrt{h^2-r_1^2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"741\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/7/4a79547a562665a63e76258bf50ba02bd041493f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1=\\frac{20\\sqrt{2}+12\\sqrt{3^2-1^2}}{2}=10\\sqrt{2}+12\\sqrt{2}=22\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"402\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/b/5fb219c45d40587e58b0e0d5c37272b8e34bed80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1^2=(22\\sqrt{2})^2=\\boxed{968}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"174\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~Tomas Diaz. orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_6_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018040559\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.188 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 119/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 386/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5805/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.584      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    5.584      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25884:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018040559 and revision id 205869. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}